Subject: [PATCH 04666/11362] [outer-loop] IGE-style LLM-guided Go-Explore:
 built + wired + honest n=1 A/B (no first-win lift)

Operator-directed ('let's try IGE-style LLM-guided Go-Explore'). Intelligent
Go-Explore (arXiv:2405.15143): replace the live Go-Explore archive's cell-selection
heuristic with an LLM (Qwen3.5-9B-MTP) judging which archived cell is most promising
to return-to-and-explore-from. The ONLY new lever vs the already-nulled plain archive
(exp4701/.433, exp4831/.445) and RND novelty (exp4688/.432).

DELIVERED (code landed via conductor git-add-A sweeps; this commit banks the A/B result):
- arc_ige_cell_selector.py: IGECellSelector (verifier_is_oracle=False) + coerce; LLM
  ranks cells, returns None -> archive heuristic on any failure (no fabrication).
- arc_go_explore.py: selector hook in GoExploreReplayArchive.select_prefix (heuristic
  fallback retained); coerce accepts a selector.
- arc_executable_world_model.py: LocalGGUFProposer.complete_text (raw free-text path).
- arc_competition_agent.py: SUBMITTED_IGE_CELL_SELECTION_* flag (default OFF) +
  live-path-reachable wiring + SUBMITTED_AGENT_CONFIG keys.
- scripts/experiments/arc_ige_llm_go_explore_ab.py: isolated A/B (both arms identical
  except the selector), reproduction-gated, PRECONDITION-blocks if the LLM is down.
- 16 unit tests (all assert); ruff clean+formatted; orphan-solver lint passes.

HONEST RESULT (results/arc_ige_llm_go_explore_ab.json, adversarial_verify clean):
selector EXERCISED with the real LLM (8 calls, 7 choices, 1 parse-failure -> graceful
heuristic fallback, live proof the no-fabrication path works). first-win 0.000 vs 0.000
on ar25 (n=1) -> NO first-win lift; the generation wall survives, consistent with the
triangulated .448-.452 finding. Caveat: n=1 (search-bound runs exceed the interactive
time budget); a powered multi-game A/B needs a longer detached/conductor run.

STRUCTURAL FINDING: at the SUBMITTED archive granularity (bins=6) the coarse cell key
collapses a game like ar25 to ~2 cells, so with the current-path exclusion the selector
almost never has >=2 ELIGIBLE cells to choose among -> IGE cannot help regardless of LLM
quality. The selector only fires with finer cells (bins=16 -> ~23 cells). IGE's premise
needs an archive abstraction that produces enough distinct cells.

